  "notes": "{素直|すなお} describes someone who is obedient, honest, or straightforward in their behavior or expression.\n\nForms:\n- {素直|すなお}な + noun: {素直|すなお}な{子|こ} (an obedient child)\n- {素直|すなお}に + verb: {素直|すなお}に{従|したが}う (to obey willingly)\n\nCommon collocations:\n- {素直|すなお}に{謝|あやま}る (to apologize honestly)\n- {素直|すなお}に{喜|よろこ}ぶ (to be honestly happy)\n- {素直|すなお}な{気持|きも}ち (honest feelings)\n- {素直|すなお}な{性格|せいかく} (obedient/honest personality)\n\nNuances:\n- Can be positive (honest, open) or neutral (obedient)\n- {素直|すなお}じゃない = stubborn, unwilling to be honest",
